{"_id":"wmPlayerGuide001","name":"Wrathmaker — Player Guide","ownership":{"default":2},"pages":[{"_id":"wmGuidePage00001","name":"Welcome & quick reference","type":"text","sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Welcome &amp; quick reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Your central reference for Wrathmaker's additions to Pathfinder 2e. Use the journal's page list to jump to a topic. These are campaign house rules, not replacements for every PF2e rule.</p><p>The tables show the module's current defaults. Your character sheet, item and Workbench show your campaign's configured values; ask the GM if they differ. Optional features may not be enabled.</p><ul><li>Choose a profession on your character sheet; its feats appear under Profession Feats.</li><li>Track Hero Points on your character and Nephilim Points on the party.</li><li>Use the party Exploration tab for travel and the Workbench for crafting, gathering and disassembly.</li><li>Look under Pathfinder 2E Wrathmaker in Compendium Packs for the additional items, professions and guides.</li></ul><p>The Mark pages at the end include sources and descriptions. A listed Mark is a reference, not an automatic grant: your item and artisan must qualify.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00002","name":"Professions & specialisations","type":"text","sort":200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Professions &amp; specialisations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Choose one starting profession at level 1. It grants its named Lore, Additional Lore, Specialty Crafting and its determined bonus feat. Profession Feats are grouped beneath their parent profession.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Profession</th><th>Additional feat</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blacksmithing</td><td>Quick Repair</td></tr><tr><td>Alchemy</td><td>Alchemical Crafting</td></tr><tr><td>Enchanting</td><td>Magical Crafting</td></tr><tr><td>Leatherwork</td><td>Experienced Tracker</td></tr><tr><td>Carpentry</td><td>Hefty Hauler</td></tr><tr><td>Stonemasonry</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Glassmaking</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Pottery</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Weaving</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Bookmaking</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Tailoring</td><td>To be determined</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Lore proficiency is trained at level 1, expert at 3, master at 7 and legendary at 15. At levels 4, 10 and 16, choose a specialty of your starting profession or learn a new profession. Specialty Lore follows the same proficiency progression.</p><p>Relevant profession checks receive a +2 circumstance bonus. This does not stack with another circumstance bonus such as Specialty Crafting on the same check. Each specialisation has Signature, Mastery and Legacy sections; use its current description, and do not treat unresolved placeholders as granted benefits.</p><h2>Blacksmithing</h2><ul><li><strong>Hellforging</strong>: Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</li><li><strong>Radiant Forging</strong>: Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</li><li><strong>Azlanti Artifice</strong>: Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</li></ul><h2>Alchemy</h2><ul><li><strong>Grand Apothecary</strong>: Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</li><li><strong>Venomcraft</strong>: Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</li><li><strong>Transmutative Alchemy</strong>: Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</li></ul><h2>Enchanting</h2><ul><li><strong>Aethercasting</strong>: Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</li><li><strong>Essencebinding</strong>: Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</li><li><strong>Runecarving</strong>: Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</li></ul><h2>Leatherwork</h2><ul><li><strong>Wyrmcraft</strong>: Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</li><li><strong>Beastbinding</strong>: Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</li><li><strong>Mantlecraft</strong>: Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</li></ul><h2>Carpentry</h2><ul><li><strong>Warbowyer</strong>: Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</li><li><strong>Masterwright</strong>: Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</li><li><strong>Warcarving</strong>: Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</li></ul><h2>Stonemasonry</h2><ul><li><strong>Megalithics</strong>: Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</li><li><strong>Runemasonry</strong>: Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</li><li><strong>Titanmasonry</strong>: Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</li></ul><h2>Glassmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Prismcraft</strong>: Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</li><li><strong>Mirrorcraft</strong>: Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</li><li><strong>Aetherglass</strong>: Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</li></ul><h2>Pottery</h2><ul><li><strong>Ceramancy</strong>: Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</li><li><strong>Reliquarycraft</strong>: Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</li><li><strong>Pyroceramics</strong>: Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</li></ul><h2>Weaving</h2><ul><li><strong>Aetherweaving</strong>: Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</li><li><strong>Ironweaving</strong>: Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</li><li><strong>Heraldweaving</strong>: Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</li></ul><h2>Bookmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Grimoirecraft</strong>: Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</li><li><strong>Chroniclecraft</strong>: Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</li><li><strong>Grand Cartography</strong>: Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</li></ul><h2>Tailoring</h2><ul><li><strong>Battlestitching</strong>: Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</li><li><strong>Veilcraft</strong>: Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</li><li><strong>Regaliacraft</strong>: Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</li></ul></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00003","name":"Hero & Nephilim Points","type":"text","sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Hero &amp; Nephilim Points</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Hero Points</h2><p>You can hold up to 10 Hero Points. Unspent points carry over between sessions. Use the normal character-sheet control; ordinary Hero Point spending rules still apply unless your GM says otherwise.</p><h2>Nephilim Points</h2><p>The party has a separate shared tracker from 0 to 10 in its header. These points persist with the party. Wrathmaker tracks the total but does not define automatic powers or spending benefits; your GM explains when they are earned or spent.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00004","name":"Equipment, Core materials & Apex items","type":"text","sort":400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Equipment, Core materials &amp; Apex items</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>A crafted item combines a PF2e base item, a Core material and optional Artisan Marks. Core progression replaces rune-style progression on that item; do not add the replaced rune benefits a second time.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Weapon attack</th><th>Extra damage dice</th><th>Spell attack / DC</th><th>Armor AC / saves</th><th>Capacity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>+0</td><td>0</td><td>+0</td><td>+0 / +0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>+1</td><td>1</td><td>+1</td><td>+1 / +1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>+2</td><td>2</td><td>+2</td><td>+2 / +2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>+3</td><td>2</td><td>+3</td><td>+3 / +3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>+4</td><td>3</td><td>+4</td><td>+4 / +4</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>+5</td><td>4</td><td>+5</td><td>+5 / +5</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Weapon dice are additional dice, not flat damage. Shields gain +3 Hardness and +30 HP per Core progression step. The displayed item includes applicable modifications.</p><h2>Spell Focus</h2><p>A held Metal or Wood focus grants its Core spellcasting bonus to spell attacks and DCs, not spell damage, slots or proficiency. Only the strongest held focus applies.</p><h2>Dragon Scales</h2><p>Scales enhance Metal or Leather/Hide armor. Hatchling, Juvenile, Youth, Adult, Ancient and Arch Dragon grant default resistance values 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20. Black grants acid, Blue electricity, Green poison, Red fire and White cold resistance while the armor is equipped.</p><h2>Apex ability equipment</h2><p>Wrathmaker's 30 worn items grant +1 to +5 to Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma. Wear and invest the item, then use its circled A on the character sheet. Different attributes can be active together; for the same attribute only the strongest applies. Belts, rings, amulets, circlets, sashes and brooches form the collection. These are campaign rewards, not a priced shop list.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00005","name":"Resource catalogue","type":"text","sort":500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Resource catalogue</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Resources are Equipment with the Precious tag. Each inventory unit is one Resource Unit, including named lots of crystals or scales. Five units weigh 1 Bulk; ten weigh 2 Bulk. Prices below are full unit values, before a sale discount. Existing older inventory copies may still appear as Treasure.</p><p>Tier levels are 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20, with default level-based DCs 15, 19, 24, 30, 35 and 40. The actual attempt may have an adjustment.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Tier</th><th>Level</th><th>Unit value</th><th>Unit Bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Iron Ingot</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Steel Ingot</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Cold Iron Ingot</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Mithril Ingot</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adamantium Ingot</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Dark Iron Ingot</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Softwood Lumber</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardwood Lumber</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Blackwood Lumber</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Darkmoon Lumber</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starwood Lumber</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Godwood Lumber</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Fieldstone Block</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Granite Block</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Obsidian Block</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Runestone Block</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Celestite Block</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldstone Block</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Rawhide Sheet</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardened Leather Sheet</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ironhide Sheet</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonhide Sheet</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Titanhide Sheet</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Primordial Hide Sheet</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Greenleaf Bundle</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Embercap Bundle</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ghostmoss Bundle</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonbloom Bundle</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starspore Bundle</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldroot Bundle</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Faint Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Charged Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Resonant Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arcane Prisms (10)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Astral Crystals (10)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Aetherheart Crystals (10)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr></tbody></table></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00006","name":"Crafting in the Workbench","type":"text","sort":600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Crafting in the Workbench</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><ol><li>Choose the party, drop a supported base item into Craft, and select its recipe, Core material and Tier.</li><li>Add one lead artisan. Every supported recipe can be crafted solo. Additional material specialists unlock their eligible Marks and combinations rather than access to the base item.</li><li>Choose Marks and compatible Anchors. Review materials, Capacity and required progress.</li><li>Create the project to reserve Party Stash stock. Reservations prevent promising the same stock to multiple projects; they do not consume it.</li><li>Commit downtime and resolve Work Blocks. At completion, review and confirm the resource consumption and finished item.</li></ol><h2>Working together</h2><p>Up to six distinct artisans contribute. Each spends the same calendar downtime. A successful one-day block produces one Progress per artisan: six artisans produce six Progress. For a block of D days (1–5), success gives D Progress per artisan; critical success gives ceiling(1.5 × D); failure gives zero for one day or floor(D ÷ 2) for longer blocks; critical failure gives zero. Time estimates assume success.</p><p>Cancel a project to release unspent reservations. Archive finished projects to keep the list manageable. Deleting a record does not refund spent materials. Report a missing finished item to the GM rather than crafting a duplicate.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00007","name":"Artisan Marks & activations","type":"text","sort":700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Artisan Marks &amp; activations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Click an artisan to choose Marks. Sources identify the profession and specialisation. Item compatibility, Anchors, minimum Tiers, stock and stacking rules still apply; extra artisans do not automatically activate every synergy.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Capacity cost</th><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Minor</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Major</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Superior</td><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Mark is allowed per item. Capacity is shared across all artisans. Secondary structural material must normally be at least Core Tier minus two. Some Marks impose stricter requirements.</p><p>Make & Marks on the finished item records the Core, applied Marks and makers. Chat badges provide compact provenance. Structure-only and consumable-only Marks do not appear in the equipment picker.</p><p>Some numerical effects are automated, others require their condition to be selected or resolved during play. For explicit action costs, Add Mark Actions to Wielder creates native action entries on the owning character. These post the rules; they do not automatically resolve targets, damage or limited uses. An unspecified action cost is not permission to activate for free. Remove a linked action when its item is lost or transferred.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00008","name":"Gathering & disassembly","type":"text","sort":800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Gathering &amp; disassembly</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Gather</h2><p>Use the Workbench Gather tab. Select a character, environment and resource; review its Tier, skill, DC, time and expected yield, then attempt the check. Region and environment can restrict available goods. Rewards go to the party or gathering character according to your campaign settings.</p><h2>Disassemble</h2><p>Drop a Wrathmaker-formatted item from your sheet or Party Stash into Disassemble. Review returns before confirming: the item is destroyed. Default recovery is 90%, rounded down separately for each material, Tier and variant. Recorded items use their project ledger; other compatible items show a standard-recipe estimate. Returns go to the selected Party Stash. Dismantled items cannot be salvaged twice or recovered as missing outputs.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00009","name":"Flanking","type":"text","sort":900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Flanking</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>First establish a normal opposite-side flank with two qualifying melee combatants in reach. Additional qualifying combatants can contribute from other sides.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Qualifying combatants</th><th>Final target AC penalty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>−2: Off-guard (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>−3: Outnumbered (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>4 or more</td><td>−4: Surrounded (Flanked)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are final penalties, not additions to the normal −2. Only qualifying melee attacks benefit; ranged attacks do not inherit this flanking penalty. Reach weapons count when they can reach the target. A creature unable to flank or an immune target follows its normal restrictions.</p><p>If the target is more than one size category larger than the largest qualifying flanker, the enhanced thresholds become six for −3 and eight for −4. A normal two-person flank still gives −2.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00010","name":"Party travel & exploration","type":"text","sort":1000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Party travel &amp; exploration</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>The party's Exploration tab combines normal exploration activities with travel setup, rider assignments and the daily plan. On foot, the slowest member limits shared Speed. Vehicle riders use transport Speed, while walkers can still slow the group. Pulled transport uses the slowest selected hauler, subject to the vehicle limit.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Shared Speed</th><th>Activities per day</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10 feet or less</td><td>½ (one activity over two days)</td></tr><tr><td>15–25 feet</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>30–40 feet</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>45–55 feet</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>60 feet or more</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Assign Travel, Reconnoiter, Fortify Camp, Map the Area, Subsist or Other and mark activities Used as they finish. Save Travel Plan preserves choices; Begin Day & Share posts the plan. The sun button starts a new day.</p><h2>Express Rider house rule</h2><p>Select the character rolling Nature, pulling creatures and up to six affected party travellers, including walkers. The check uses the highest selected Will DC. Success or critical success increases affected overland Speeds by half for that day. Unaffected walkers and vehicle limits still constrain the group. This changes overland travel, not encounter Speed.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00011","name":"Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Hellforging</h2><p>Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</p><h3>Signature — Infernal Temper</h3><p>Create Hellforged equipment built around fire, blood, fear, retaliation and dangerous power.</p><h3>Mastery — Furnace Without Mercy</h3><p>Reduce Hellforging special-resource cost by 20%; at high tier recover 50% of rare infernal components from dismantled Hellforged gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Infernal Foundry</h3><p>Supports elite army weapons, infernal siege ammunition and intimidating military infrastructure.</p><h2>Radiant Forging</h2><p>Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</p><h3>Signature — Radiant Temper</h3><p>Create protective, cleansing and celestial equipment, especially effective against undead, fiends and corruption.</p><h3>Mastery — Purified Forge</h3><p>Reduce sacred/celestial resource waste by 20% and improve repairs to Radiant equipment.</p><h3>Legacy — Beacon Works</h3><p>Supports hospitals, temples, settlement wards, anti-undead defences and sacred military equipment.</p><h2>Azlanti Artifice</h2><p>Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</p><h3>Signature — Lost Artifice</h3><p>Reverse-engineer ancient technology, repair magitek and invent designs beyond normal PF2e equipment lists.</p><h3>Mastery — Reverse Engineering</h3><p>Preserve the original device while producing a reusable blueprint; repeat builds take 25% less downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Industrialisation</h3><p>Enables automated workshops, magical power, transport, constructs and advanced siege technology.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00012","name":"Alchemy — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Alchemy — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Grand Apothecary</h2><p>Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</p><h3>Signature — Refined Formula</h3><p>Customise medicines, potions and elixirs for potency, duration, administration and recovery.</p><h3>Mastery — Batch Distillation</h3><p>Produce 25% more doses from the same material input.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Apothecary</h3><p>Supports hospitals, military medicine, plague response and settlement recovery.</p><h2>Venomcraft</h2><p>Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</p><h3>Signature — Toxin Refinement</h3><p>Customise poisons by delivery, onset, target profile, stages and concealment.</p><h3>Mastery — Venom Harvesting</h3><p>Gain 25% more usable poison material from venomous creatures and reduce poison resource cost by 15%.</p><h3>Legacy — Master Toxicologist</h3><p>Supports antivenom, pest control, military toxins and intelligence operations.</p><h2>Transmutative Alchemy</h2><p>Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</p><h3>Signature — Material Transmutation</h3><p>Convert resource families and create composite materials for other artisans.</p><h3>Mastery — The Great Work</h3><p>Standard conversion is 2 units into 1 equal-tier unit; mastered high-tier conversions can improve to 3 into 2.</p><h3>Legacy — Transmutation Industry</h3><p>Converts surplus Kingdom resources and enables specialised industrial projects.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00013","name":"Enchanting — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Enchanting — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Aethercasting</h2><p>Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</p><h3>Signature — Empowerment</h3><p>Create statistic-enhancing and magically sustained equipment that can intentionally push beyond ordinary PF2e ceilings.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Refinement</h3><p>Upgrade an existing Empowerment by paying only the material difference and half normal upgrade downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Permanent Enchantment</h3><p>Supports wards, magical utilities, powered workshops and settlement infrastructure.</p><h2>Essencebinding</h2><p>Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</p><h3>Signature — Bind Essence</h3><p>Add traits and supernatural creature/material properties the base item does not normally possess.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Binding</h3><p>Higher-tier work supports stronger creature-derived properties and more complex essence interactions.</p><h3>Legacy — Essence Workshops</h3><p>Converts monster, planar and environmental essences into reusable crafting components.</p><h2>Runecarving</h2><p>Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</p><h3>Signature — Runic Logic</h3><p>Build persistent sigils and linked magical logic into equipment; this replaces the old assumption that normal PF2e property runes still exist.</p><h3>Mastery — Rune Resonance</h3><p>Linked sigils are easier to upgrade and can interact across paired items.</p><h3>Legacy — Runic Infrastructure</h3><p>Supports ward arrays, military sigils and public magical systems.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00014","name":"Leatherwork — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Leatherwork — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Wyrmcraft</h2><p>Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</p><h3>Signature — Draconic Essence</h3><p>Preserve and exploit qualities from dragon type, colour and age in armour, weapons and reinforcement. Dragon Scale Core and Reinforcement already provide native colour resistance; Wyrmcraft deepens or transforms that inheritance.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Harvest</h3><p>Gain more usable dragon material and reduce waste while preparing scales and hides.</p><h3>Legacy — Dragonworks</h3><p>Creates elite army equipment, prestige goods, diplomatic trophies and draconic settlement works.</p><h2>Beastbinding</h2><p>Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</p><h3>Signature — Preserve the Beast</h3><p>Retain a natural or supernatural quality from the creature whose hide/material was used.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Harvester</h3><p>Improve creature-material yield and preserve delicate traits that ordinary harvesting would destroy.</p><h3>Legacy — Monstercraft Trade</h3><p>Turns rare creature materials into specialist exports and campaign resources.</p><h2>Mantlecraft</h2><p>Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</p><h3>Signature — Great Mantles</h3><p>Create exceptional cloaks, coats, ceremonial furs and environmental garments.</p><h3>Mastery — Luxury Craftsmanship</h3><p>Reduce rare-fur waste and substantially increase trade/prestige value.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Clothier</h3><p>Supports diplomacy, gifts, court prestige and luxury industry.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00015","name":"Carpentry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Carpentry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Warbowyer</h2><p>Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</p><h3>Signature — Engineered Ranged Weapons</h3><p>Build bows, crossbows, ballistae, specialist ammunition and advanced loading mechanisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Fletching</h3><p>Produce ammunition efficiently and maintain engineered ranged weapons with reduced waste.</p><h3>Legacy — Missile Industry</h3><p>Improves army archers, towers, ballistae and settlement ranged defence.</p><h2>Masterwright</h2><p>Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Build bridges, roads, palisades, docks, towers, camps and major wooden infrastructure.</p><h3>Mastery — Efficient Construction</h3><p>Reduce Lumber cost and repair downtime for qualifying projects.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Builder</h3><p>Improves construction throughput, roads, fortifications, settlement expansion and repairs.</p><h2>Warcarving</h2><p>Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</p><h3>Signature — Carved Form</h3><p>Add combat identities and totemic properties to wooden weapons, shields and tools.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Carving</h3><p>Preserve increasingly complex magical/totemic carvings without weakening the wood.</p><h3>Legacy — Carved Traditions</h3><p>Supports ceremonial weapons, military equipment and cultural relics.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00016","name":"Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Megalithics</h2><p>Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Create fortresses, roads, aqueducts, monumental walls, towers and vast stone projects.</p><h3>Mastery — Monumental Engineering</h3><p>Reduce Stone waste and repair time for major works.</p><h3>Legacy — Civilisation Builder</h3><p>Transforms settlements through enduring infrastructure and wonders.</p><h2>Runemasonry</h2><p>Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</p><h3>Signature — Wardstones</h3><p>Bind magical zones, alarms, protections and restrictions to locations rather than carried items.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Inscription</h3><p>Increase ward area, duration and magical stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Wards</h3><p>Protects settlements from intrusion, teleportation, undead, weather and magical assault.</p><h2>Titanmasonry</h2><p>Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</p><h3>Signature — Titanic Construction</h3><p>Create stone armour, colossal shields, siege devices, constructs and crushing wargear.</p><h3>Mastery — Mountaincraft</h3><p>Make enormous stone components usable without losing impossible stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Stone Legions</h3><p>Supports constructs, fortifications and siege warfare.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00017","name":"Glassmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Glassmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Prismcraft</h2><p>Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</p><h3>Signature — Arcane Optics</h3><p>Focus, split, redirect and transform light or magical energy with precision lenses and prisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Refraction</h3><p>Safely handle stronger magical energy and reduce material loss in advanced optical components.</p><h3>Legacy — Observatory Craft</h3><p>Supports surveying, astronomy, navigation, signalling and watchtowers.</p><h2>Mirrorcraft</h2><p>Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</p><h3>Signature — Reflection</h3><p>Create supernatural mirrors for illusion, scrying, communication, defence and travel.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Reflection</h3><p>Safely reflect or retain increasingly powerful magical phenomena.</p><h3>Legacy — Mirror Network</h3><p>Links settlements for communication, intelligence and eventually transport.</p><h2>Aetherglass</h2><p>Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</p><h3>Signature — Mana Conduction</h3><p>Build mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry and construct cores.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Cells</h3><p>Store progressively greater magical energy with less loss and safer discharge.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Grid</h3><p>Powers large-scale magical infrastructure and magitek networks.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00018","name":"Pottery — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Pottery — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Ceramancy</h2><p>Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</p><h3>Signature — Living Clay</h3><p>Create supernatural ceramics, terracotta guardians and adaptive ceramic armour.</p><h3>Mastery — Awakened Kiln</h3><p>Build increasingly complex animated ceramics with less breakage and better control.</p><h3>Legacy — Terracotta Works</h3><p>Supports workers, guardians, soldiers and settlement sentinels.</p><h2>Reliquarycraft</h2><p>Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</p><h3>Signature — Vessel of Essence</h3><p>Capture and safely preserve supernatural essences, spirits, curses, blessings and planar energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Containment</h3><p>Safely house stronger and more volatile essences with less risk of leakage or corruption.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Reliquaries</h3><p>Supports temples, magical institutions, cursed-artifact storage and spirit containment.</p><h2>Pyroceramics</h2><p>Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</p><h3>Signature — Cruciblecraft</h3><p>Create bomb casings, furnaces, crucibles, pressure vessels and extreme-temperature components.</p><h3>Mastery — Grand Kiln</h3><p>Improve industrial/alchemical throughput and reduce failures when processing extreme heat materials.</p><h3>Legacy — Industrial Kilns</h3><p>Supports bricks, pipes, sanitation, forges, alchemy and mass production.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00019","name":"Weaving — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Weaving — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Aetherweaving</h2><p>Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</p><h3>Signature — Manathread</h3><p>Produce magically conductive fabric capable of storing, carrying and shaping supernatural energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Loom</h3><p>Weave stronger magical fibres and exotic feedstocks without losing their properties.</p><h3>Legacy — Magical Textile Industry</h3><p>Supports magical garments, banners, specialist exports and arcane infrastructure.</p><h2>Ironweaving</h2><p>Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</p><h3>Signature — Warcloth</h3><p>Produce armour backing, nets, ropes, strings, sails and flexible reinforcement designed for combat stress.</p><h3>Mastery — Steel Thread</h3><p>Integrate stronger materials without sacrificing flexibility.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Textiles</h3><p>Supports armour, siege gear, sails, ropes and army equipment.</p><h2>Heraldweaving</h2><p>Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Great Standards</h3><p>Create banners and tapestries that carry morale, identity and supernatural command presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Living Heraldry</h3><p>Standards grow more potent when tied to a recognised army, ruler, settlement or company.</p><h3>Legacy — National Identity</h3><p>Supports armies, festivals, loyalty, diplomacy and prestige.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00020","name":"Bookmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Bookmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Grimoirecraft</h2><p>Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</p><h3>Signature — Living Grimoires</h3><p>Create spellbooks and codices that interact directly with spell preparation, memory and magical resonance.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Codex</h3><p>Improve magical capacity, indexing and stability while reducing time to expand or revise the grimoire.</p><h3>Legacy — Grand Academies</h3><p>Supports magical education, spell research and institutional knowledge.</p><h2>Chroniclecraft</h2><p>Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</p><h3>Signature — Codices of Mastery</h3><p>Record Lore, formulae, techniques and expertise precisely enough that others can temporarily benefit from it.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Instruction</h3><p>Preserve increasingly advanced knowledge while reducing training/research time.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Library</h3><p>Improves research, education, formula preservation and Culture.</p><h2>Grand Cartography</h2><p>Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</p><h3>Signature — Master Atlas</h3><p>Create maps that record resources, hazards, routes, magical phenomena and strategic terrain.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Survey</h3><p>Reveal hidden resources and improve route accuracy with less exploration time.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Survey</h3><p>Improves hex claims, roads, army movement, settlement placement and resource exploitation.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00021","name":"Tailoring — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Tailoring — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Battlestitching</h2><p>Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</p><h3>Signature — War Garments</h3><p>Create combat robes, coats, armour liners, harnesses and flexible protection.</p><h3>Mastery — Combat Cut</h3><p>Increase protection without sacrificing movement and reduce material waste when refitting worn gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Tailoring</h3><p>Supports elite uniforms, armour liners and specialised army equipment.</p><h2>Veilcraft</h2><p>Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</p><h3>Signature — Impossible Garments</h3><p>Manipulate sight, sound, shadow, identity and supernatural concealment through clothing.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Veil</h3><p>Improve disguise/concealment reliability and reduce the signs left by supernatural garments.</p><h3>Legacy — Shadow Service</h3><p>Supports scouts, spies, diplomats and intelligence networks.</p><h2>Regaliacraft</h2><p>Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Vestments of Authority</h3><p>Create royal, diplomatic, ceremonial and command garments that reinforce office and presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Regalia</h3><p>Regalia becomes stronger when properly tied to a recognised office, ruler or institution.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Court</h3><p>Improves diplomacy, loyalty, leadership, festivals, prestige and foreign relations.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000001","name":"Tempered Construction — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":3000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tempered Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>+10% item HP and +1 Hardness.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000002","name":"Perfect Balance — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":3100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Balance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 1 where sensible; weapon gains +1 Artisan bonus to one chosen Athletics manoeuvre made with it.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000003","name":"Reinforced Edge — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":3200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>+1 damage per weapon damage die against objects/Hardness; +2 per die at T5+.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000004","name":"Fortified Frame — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":3300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Fortified Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Armour or shield gains +2 Hardness and +20% item HP.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000005","name":"Master Reforge — Blacksmithing — Universal","type":"text","sort":3400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Master Reforge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Universal</p><p>Recover 75% of ordinary/resource components when rebuilding and preserve compatible Wrathmaker work where physically possible.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000006","name":"Ember Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":3500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Ember Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Weapon sheds controllable light; on a critical hit deal extra fire damage equal to Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000007","name":"Blood Temper — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":3600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Blood Temper</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>While at or below half HP, deal +2 damage; +4 at Core T5+.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000008","name":"Hellfire Channel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":3700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Hellfire Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once per encounter for 1 minute, weapon deals +1d6 fire at T2–3, +2d6 at T4–5, +3d6 at T6; half ignores fire resistance.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000009","name":"Tormentor's Edge — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":3800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Tormentor&#39;s Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Critical hits force a Will save vs wielder DC; failure frightened 1, critical failure frightened 2.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000010","name":"Perfected Killing Edge — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":3900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfected Killing Edge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Weapon gains +1 attack beyond Core Material progression. Does not stack with another Over-Potency effect.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000011","name":"Soul-Burned Steel — Blacksmithing — Hellforging","type":"text","sort":4000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Soul-Burned Steel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Hellforging</p><p>Once/day when wielder would reach 0 HP, remain at 1 HP and immediately Step then Strike; afterwards become drained 1 until daily preparations.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000012","name":"Consecrated Finish — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Consecrated Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Item counts as sanctified for campaign interactions and grants +1 Artisan bonus to identify undead/fiends while worn or wielded.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000013","name":"Dawnbound — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dawnbound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Weapon deals +1 spirit damage per weapon damage die to undead and fiends.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000014","name":"Guardian's Radiance — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Guardian&#39;s Radiance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Once per round when an adjacent ally takes damage, reduce it by 2 + Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000015","name":"Aegis of Dawn — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aegis of Dawn</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Wearer gains permanent Max HP equal to 4 × Core Tier and +1 resistance to spirit/void damage per Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000016","name":"Martyr's Forge — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Martyr&#39;s Forge</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Reaction once/encounter: take damage equal to twice your level to reduce damage to an ally within 15 ft by four times your level.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>reaction</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000017","name":"Solar Ascension — Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging","type":"text","sort":4600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Solar Ascension</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute, 20-ft aura: allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to AC and saves; undead/fiends take spirit damage equal to twice Core Tier at start of their turns.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000018","name":"Diagnostic Matrix — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":4700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Diagnostic Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Item reports its condition; +2 Artisan bonus to Repair and Identify checks involving it.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000019","name":"Integrated Conduit — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":4800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Integrated Conduit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Item can house one Mana or Aetherglass component without increasing ordinary component Bulk/space.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000020","name":"Adaptive Configuration — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":4900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Configuration</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Choose two approved configurations at creation; one Interact action switches between them, such as damage type, weapon mode or tool function.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000021","name":"Arcane Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":5000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Add one once-per-encounter activated ability roughly appropriate to the item&#39;s tier/level and theme.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000022","name":"Phase Mechanism — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":5100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phase Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Once/encounter, wielder Steps or Strides up to half Speed through creatures and non-magical obstacles as if incorporeal; must end in open space.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000023","name":"Reality Engine — Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice","type":"text","sort":5200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reality Engine</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute, item can maintain two mutually exclusive configurations simultaneously or ignore one normal activation prerequisite approved at creation.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, mechanism, fittings, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): metal</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000024","name":"Stable Formula — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":5300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Consumable remains potent twice as long and ignores the first normal environmental spoilage event.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000025","name":"Efficient Batch — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":5400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Batch</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Produce +10% doses, rounded down; minimum +1 when crafting 4+ items.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000026","name":"Refined Reagent — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":5500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Reagent</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Increase one non-attack numerical consumable effect by 10%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000027","name":"Quick Preparation — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":5600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Quick Preparation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>Reduce batch downtime by 20%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000028","name":"Catalyst Reserve — Alchemy — Universal","type":"text","sort":5700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Catalyst Reserve</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Universal</p><p>When used as a component in another project, reduce one secondary resource requirement by 10%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000029","name":"Measured Dose — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":5800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Measured Dose</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Remove one minor drawback or reduce a fixed consumable drawback by 25%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000030","name":"Concentrated — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":5900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Concentrated</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Increase healing or temporary HP from the consumable by 25%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000031","name":"Extended Formula — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":6000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Extended Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Double a duration of 1 minute or longer, maximum 24 hours unless the GM approves more.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000032","name":"Rapid Infusion — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":6100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Infusion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Draw and drink/administer this consumable as a single action.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>consumable</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>action 1</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000033","name":"Restorative Panacea — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":6200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Restorative Panacea</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>In addition to normal effect, reduce two of clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, sickened or stupefied by 1 and attempt one counteract check vs poison/disease/curse.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000034","name":"Phoenix Draught — Alchemy — Grand Apothecary","type":"text","sort":6300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Phoenix Draught</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Grand Apothecary</p><p>Once/day per creature, if consumed while above 0 HP it remains active for 1 hour; first time the creature would fall to 0 HP, it instead remains at 1 HP and gains temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000035","name":"Masked Toxin — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Masked Toxin</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to the poison&#39;s DC against attempts to detect it before exposure.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000036","name":"Adhesive Poison — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adhesive Poison</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>A failed Strike does not consume an applied injury poison; it remains until a successful Strike or the encounter ends.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000037","name":"Swift Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Swift Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Reduce onset by one step; if no onset, failed initial save immediately applies Stage 1 before normal progression.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000038","name":"Predator Formula — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator Formula</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Choose one creature family when crafted; poison DC gains +2 Artisan bonus against that family.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000039","name":"Mutagenic Venom — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Mutagenic Venom</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Add one approved Stage 3 rider such as slowed 1, stupefied 2 or enfeebled 2 for 1 round.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000040","name":"Perfect Killer — Alchemy — Venomcraft","type":"text","sort":6900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Killer</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Venomcraft</p><p>Poison gains +1 DC beyond its normal item/tier DC and treats the first successful save against it as a failure once per target.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000041","name":"Purified Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Purified Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Remove one undesirable mundane tag or impurity from a component.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000042","name":"Alchemical Alloy — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Alchemical Alloy</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Component gains one approved material tag from a second same-tier material used in its creation.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000043","name":"Composite Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Composite Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Component can satisfy two compatible resource-family requirements while occupying one component position.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000044","name":"Refined Substance — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Refined Substance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>For one named Artisan Mark, treat this component as 1 Tier higher, maximum effective T6; does not raise Core progression.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000045","name":"Philosopher's Matrix — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Philosopher&#39;s Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>Once per project, substitute one missing non-unique resource family with equal quantity of another same-tier family.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000046","name":"Living Transmutation — Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy","type":"text","sort":7500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Transmutation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy</p><p>During daily preparations choose one of two pre-built material identities for the component; switch its native tags and compatible specialist hooks until next preparations.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>project</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, reagent, catalyst, lining</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): herbs</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000047","name":"Stable Matrix — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":7600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stable Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus when resisting suppression/counteraction of the item&#39;s custom magic.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000048","name":"Attuned Craft — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":7700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Attuned Craft</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Key custom activations to a wielder, tradition, deity, element or other approved identity.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000049","name":"Resonant Channel — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":7800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Channel</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>+1 charge to one custom daily charge pool, maximum +1 from this Mark.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000050","name":"Efficient Activation — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":7900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Efficient Activation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Once per encounter, reduce one approved 2-action custom item activation to 1 action.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000051","name":"Arcane Safeguard — Enchanting — Universal","type":"text","sort":8000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Arcane Safeguard</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Universal</p><p>Reduce damage/penalties from a custom item overload or critical activation failure by 50%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000052","name":"Minor Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to one narrow skill use/subcategory agreed at creation.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000053","name":"Focused Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Focused Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to one selected secondary statistic such as initiative, a skill, or a specific save against one effect family.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000054","name":"Twin Empowerment — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Twin Empowerment</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Choose two different secondary statistics; each gains +1 Artisan bonus while attuned.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000055","name":"Overcharged Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overcharged Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Once/encounter for 1 round, increase one existing Artisan numerical bonus on the item by +1.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000056","name":"Overlord Matrix — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Overlord Matrix</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Choose weapon attack or spell attack/DC when crafted; gain +1 beyond Core progression in that category. Does not stack with another Over-Potency effect.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000057","name":"Aetherheart Lattice — Enchanting — Aethercasting","type":"text","sort":8600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Aetherheart Lattice</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Aethercasting</p><p>Gain 2 charges/day; spend 1 to refresh one once-per-encounter Standard/Major activation on the item, or at start of turn gain temp HP equal to 2 × Core Tier if below half HP.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000058","name":"Minor Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":8700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Minor Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Add one non-combat descriptive/material trait or approved utility tag.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000059","name":"Bound Trait — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":8800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bound Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Add one approved item/weapon trait such as shove, trip, disarm, modular or versatile.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000060","name":"Elemental Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":8900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Elemental Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Weapon deals +1d6 acid/cold/electricity/fire at T2–3, +2d6 at T4–5, +3d6 at T6; defensive items instead grant resistance equal to 2 × Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000061","name":"Predatory Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":9000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predatory Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Bind one source-derived sense or movement mode such as scent 30 ft, climb 15 ft, swim 20 ft or darkvision.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000062","name":"Greater Binding — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":9100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Greater Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Add one strong source-derived property such as reach extension, a once-per-encounter special attack, or comparable extraordinary trait approved by GM.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000063","name":"Living Essence — Enchanting — Essencebinding","type":"text","sort":9200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Essence</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Essencebinding</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute the item awakens and manifests one high-tier transformation/ability based on the bound essence.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000064","name":"Runic Signature — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Signature</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify, repair or modify sigils made by this artisan.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000065","name":"Resonant Pair — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Resonant Pair</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Link two crafted items; while within 30 ft each bearer gains +1 Artisan bonus to saves against effects created by the other&#39;s current target.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000066","name":"Layered Inscription — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Layered Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Choose one Standard Mark on the item; it can be toggled between two pre-defined modes during daily preparations.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000067","name":"Runic Feedback — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Runic Feedback</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Once/encounter when a linked weapon critically hits, paired item grants +2 Artisan bonus to its next attack, save or activation check before end of next turn.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000068","name":"Living Rune — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Living Rune</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>One Major-or-lower custom effect on the item may switch between two equal-power versions with a single action once per encounter.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000069","name":"Grand Glyph — Enchanting — Runecarving","type":"text","sort":9800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Glyph</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Enchanting — Runecarving</p><p>Once/day place a 15-ft rune zone for 1 minute that reproduces one approved Standard/Major defensive or offensive item effect for allies/enemies in the area.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, catalyst, lens, frame</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): mana-crystals, stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000070","name":"Flexible Construction — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":9900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Flexible Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Reduce one movement-related armour penalty by 1 where applicable.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000071","name":"Perfect Fit — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":10000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfect Fit</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 1 for worn leather/hide equipment and remove minor fitting penalties.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000072","name":"Reinforced Hide — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":10100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Hide</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>+10% item HP and +1 Hardness; doubles at T5+.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000073","name":"Weather Seal — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":10200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weather Seal</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Wearer gains +2 Artisan bonus to saves/checks against ordinary environmental exposure covered by the garment.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000074","name":"Adaptive Strapping — Leatherwork — Universal","type":"text","sort":10300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Adaptive Strapping</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Universal</p><p>Once per round drawing/stowing one item secured to the gear is part of the same Interact action used to manipulate it.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000075","name":"Wyrm Inscription — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm Inscription</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Item visibly records source dragon; +2 Artisan bonus to identify or track lore tied to that dragon type.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000076","name":"Draconic Resistance — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Resistance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Increase the item&#39;s active native resistance by Dragon Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000077","name":"Scale Dominion — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Scale Dominion</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Armour/shield gains +2 Hardness and +15 HP per Dragon Tier; weapon instead ignores resistance equal to Dragon Tier against the associated damage type.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000078","name":"Draconic Constitution — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Draconic Constitution</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>While attuned to worn armour, gain Max HP equal to 4 × Dragon Tier and a +2 Artisan bonus to saves against effects that deal the associated damage type; Green applies to poison effects. This replaces the Mark&#39;s former extra resistance.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>armor</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000079","name":"Wyrm's Fury — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wyrm&#39;s Fury</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Weapon gains +1 additional base weapon damage die beyond Core progression. Must use Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement; does not stack with other Over-Striking.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000080","name":"Dragonheart Awakening — Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft","type":"text","sort":10900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Dragonheart Awakening</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute gain fly Speed equal to land Speed, increase the active native resistance by 2 × Dragon Tier, and gain one 30-ft cone breath weapon dealing 2d6 per Dragon Tier, basic Reflex save. This increase stacks with Draconic Resistance on the same item.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000081","name":"Trophy Memory — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Memory</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to Recall Knowledge about the source creature family while carrying/wearing the item.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000082","name":"Predator's Sense — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Sense</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Gain one source-appropriate sense such as scent 15 ft, low-light vision, or +2 Artisan bonus to tracking that creature family.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000083","name":"Natural Movement — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11200000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Natural Movement</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Gain one source-appropriate movement mode: climb 15 ft, swim 20 ft, or +10 ft Speed in a defined natural environment.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000084","name":"Apex Hide — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11300000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Hide</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>At start of combat gain temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier and +1 Artisan bonus to saves against one source-creature theme such as fear, cold, poison or grabs.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000085","name":"Apex Trait — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11400000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Apex Trait</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Gain one extraordinary source-derived trait/ability such as powerful leap, amphibious movement, tremorsense 15 ft, or comparable effect approved by GM.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000086","name":"Chimera Binding — Leatherwork — Beastbinding","type":"text","sort":11500000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Chimera Binding</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Beastbinding</p><p>Combine two compatible creature-source properties in one item; choose which is active as a free action once per round, or activate both for 1 minute once/day.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>free</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000087","name":"Trophy Finish — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":11600000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Trophy Finish</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to social checks where the displayed trophy/source is relevant to status or intimidation.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000088","name":"Weather Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":11700000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Weather Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Ignore ordinary extreme-weather penalties and gain +2 Artisan bonus to saves against severe environmental exposure.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000089","name":"Predator's Cloak — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":11800000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Predator&#39;s Cloak</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Stealth and Survival in one source-appropriate terrain; once/encounter Step 5 ft after successfully Hiding.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000090","name":"Court Mantle — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":11900000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Court Mantle</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Diplomacy and Society in formal settings; adjacent allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves against fear while wearer is conscious.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Applies to</th><td>item</td></tr><tr><th>Activation</th><td>Passive or source-defined; unspecified action costs require GM adjudication</td></tr><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): leather, dragon-scale</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"},"ownership":{"default":2}},{"_id":"wmMark0000000091","name":"Sovereign Pelt — Leatherwork — Mantlecraft","type":"text","sort":12000000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Sovereign Pelt</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Leatherwork — Mantlecraft</p><p>Gain Max HP equal to 6 × Core Tier and +2 Artisan b